§§ `Regulation 1: the definitions, as tests over an exam's facts`

-- Each limb of a definition is tested on both sides: with it and without it.  The two definitions are independent,
-- so an exam that assesses both is both.

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`an exam that assesses practical skills, taken by a learner, on the curriculum` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS TRUE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS FALSE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS TRUE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`an exam that assesses theory, taken by a learner, on the curriculum` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS FALSE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS TRUE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS TRUE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`an exam that assesses both, taken by a learner, on the curriculum` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS TRUE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS TRUE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS TRUE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`a practical exam taken by someone who is not a learner in a vocational training course` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS TRUE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS FALSE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS FALSE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`a practical exam on subjects outside the curriculum for cooling facilities` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS TRUE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS FALSE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS TRUE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`a theory exam taken by someone who is not a learner in a vocational training course` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS FALSE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS TRUE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS FALSE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
`a theory exam on subjects outside the curriculum for cooling facilities` MEANS
    `Exam in a vocational training course` WITH
        `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner` IS FALSE
        `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects` IS TRUE
        `taken by a learner in a vocational training course` IS TRUE
        `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities` IS FALSE

-- The draft defines both.
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` `an exam that assesses practical skills, taken by a learner, on the curriculum`
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` `an exam that assesses theory, taken by a learner, on the curriculum`
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` `a practical exam taken by someone who is not a learner in a vocational training course`
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` `a practical exam on subjects outside the curriculum for cooling facilities`
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` `an exam that assesses theory, taken by a learner, on the curriculum`
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` `an exam that assesses practical skills, taken by a learner, on the curriculum`
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` `a theory exam taken by someone who is not a learner in a vocational training course`
#ASSERT NOT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` `a theory exam on subjects outside the curriculum for cooling facilities`
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` `an exam that assesses both, taken by a learner, on the curriculum`
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` `an exam that assesses both, taken by a learner, on the curriculum`

-- As made, regulation 1 defines the practical exam only; a theoretical exam is not defined and the answer is a named refusal.
